  "body": "What happens: A plate has a through hole. The user picks the hole wall in 2D Contour and sets Side to Outside. The cutter centre runs 3.0 mm into the material (tool D6, 120 sampled points inside the part). The program posts with no warning. The cutting moves are only at Z=10, the top of the part.\n\nExpected: The operation is refused by name (\"Outside of a hole is inside the part - use Inside or Auto\"). Or the verifier blocks the post. A path in material is never silent.\n\nEvidence: Measured on main d1484f02a (2026-11-15), tool D6 flat end mill. All other routes put the cutter centre 3.000 mm from the wall. See #1777 for the older defect where the centre ran on the model edge, and `operations.rs:2462` `a_closed_chain_routes_the_boundary_path_not_a_centerline`.\n\nNot confirmed: why the depth stops at the top. Not confirmed: whether a deeper setting makes a real gouge that the verifier catches.\n\nDone means: A test pins the refusal or the block. The test also covers full depth.\n\nRelated: #1928, #1929\n",
